<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  OWASP Dependency-Check suppression file.

  Each <suppress> is SCOPED to a specific artifact via <packageUrl>, so the same
  CVE appearing on a DIFFERENT dependency later still fails the build. All carry
  an "until" date to force periodic re-review.

  Context (2026-08-01): every dependency below is already at its latest available
  release — upgrading further is not possible. The flagged CVEs are the 2026 NVD
  CVE-flood: disputed / not-yet-fixed-upstream / CPE over-matches against
  foundational Java libs (Spring, Tomcat, Netty, Jackson, protobuf, gRPC/OTel).
  Re-review on the "until" date; delete any entry once a fixed version ships.
-->
